# The options the dash runs with, one per line (a value goes after a space).
# Every Update now puts exactly these into FROGDASH_ARGS in /etc/default/frogdash and
# restarts the dash if they changed (tools/frogdash_setup.sh, step "Dash options"):
# nothing has to be typed on the Pi. They are checked first; a list the dash would
# refuse is not used, and System check names the problem.
# Turn one off by deleting its line or putting # in front. All of them:
#   python -m hardware.frogdash.server --help
--interface can0
--gpsd
--log-dir /var/lib/frogdash/logs
# The Terminal tab under Dash management, with sudo (November 2026, the owner's choice).
--terminal
# Reverse camera on the Pi's camera connector (docs/reverse-camera.md); its own options
# (--camera-rotate 180, --camera-keep-warm ...) go on lines after it.
# --camera
# Wi-Fi dash cam view (docs/dashcam.md).
# --dashcam
